I found a viable Track B route that the initial rejection missed, so I’m reopening the decision before treating it as final. Lemma 1 supports a native “target ribbon from prescribed roots” problem: a full level sweep touches millions of cells, while the paper’s left-to-right rank invariant lets one recover one 23-cell ribbon with at most 276 interval operations. I’m prototyping this exact construction now; it will be kept only if structure-aware guessing, the attack panel, and the oracle/G9 runs all pass.
