index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3c4fe0901d441195c61978fc45f32d007d5f10d4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,177 @@
+# Ribbon-root reconstruction generator (arXiv:2408.09272)
+
+> **Status: built and locally verified, but not shippable yet.** The required
+> OpenRouter hardening run was attempted and every redraw returned HTTP 403
+> `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` before a model answered. Those errors are
+> not model failures, so G9(b) and STEP 4 remain unproved.
+
+## Profile
+
+| field | value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
+| native domain | combinatorics |
+| object regime | finite discrete |
+| computational core | other (ordered ribbon reconstruction) |
+| certificate | integer tuple: a list of lattice-square coordinate pairs |
+| intuition | invariant — a tile keeps its left-to-right rank across levels |
+| domain essentiality | native |
+| reduction | none |
+
+## What the problem is
+
+The source is Blackburn, Chen, and Kargin,
+[*An upper bound on the per-tile entropy of ribbon tilings*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.09272).
+Definition 1 makes an `L`-ribbon a path of `L` unit lattice squares whose steps
+go north or east. An instance gives a finite region as inclusive intervals of
+cells on each diagonal level `x+y`, prescribes every root square, and marks one
+root. The answer is the complete ribbon belonging to that root.
+
+The generator samples that ribbon's north/east word first, builds a noncrossing
+family of a million or more ribbons around it, and retains the planted path.
+Lemma 1 guarantees that the prescribed roots determine exactly one tiling.
+`verify` independently rank-selects the marked ribbon, then checks exact integer
+coordinates, region membership, distinctness, north/east adjacency, and root
+order. It does not read `inst["answer"]`.
+
+## Why this is Track B, not Track A
+
+Section 1 cites Sheffield's linear-in-area algorithm for constructing a ribbon
+tiling of a simply connected region. The same section says existence for general
+regions is open; the nearby NP-completeness citation concerns 180-trominoes, not
+ribbons. There is therefore no honest Track A claim for an inverse-planted ribbon
+distribution.
+
+The honest reference algorithm is the full left-to-right level sweep from
+Sheffield/Lemma 1, with complexity `O(A)`. At the candidate hard preset it
+actually visited **45,088,768 cells** in **2.316047 s** on the measured G5 seed;
+eight G6 runs averaged 3.669101 s and solved 8/8. The compact route tracks only
+the marked tile's rank and selects that rank from the annotated intervals on
+each level. Its conservative worst-case count is **281** exact comparisons and
+endpoint additions. That mechanical-versus-compact gap is the Track B claim.
+
+The interval encoding is native but succinct: it denotes the paper's lattice
+squares exactly and `verify` operates on those squares. No graph, SAT, or
+finite-field surrogate replaces the tiling problem.
+
+## Worked demo (`seed=3`)
+
+Here is the full rendered region data for `DIFFICULTY["demo"]` (boilerplate
+definitions and output instructions are summarized below, but no instance data
+are omitted):
+
+```text
+Ribbon length L: 5
+Number of ribbons: 12
+Prescribed roots: every region square on the smallest displayed level, and no other square.
+Marked root: [-17,12]
+
+level -5: ranks 0..11: [-23,-12]
+level -4: ranks 0..0: [-23,-23]; ranks 1..11: [-21,-11]
+level -3: ranks 0..0: [-23,-23]; ranks 1..1: [-21,-21]; ranks 2..11: [-19,-10]
+level -2: ranks 0..0: [-23,-23]; ranks 1..1: [-21,-21]; ranks 2..7: [-19,-14]; ranks 8..11: [-12,-9]
+level -1: ranks 0..0: [-23,-23]; ranks 1..1: [-21,-21]; ranks 2..5: [-19,-16]; ranks 6..7: [-14,-13]; ranks 8..11: [-11,-8]
+```
+
+Each interval `[a,b]` on level `l` contains exactly the cells `[x,l-x]` for
+`a <= x <= b`. Following rank 6 from the marked root gives:
+
+```json
+[[-17,12],[-16,12],[-15,12],[-15,13],[-14,13]]
+```
+
+`verify(inst, answer)` returns `(True, "ok")`. Dropping its last square returns
+`(False, "wrong path length: expected 5 squares")`. A person can solve this
+demo on paper by following one rank through five short interval lists.
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| preset | roots / level (`n`) | ribbon length | full-sweep cell visits | status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 12 | 5 | 60 | hand example |
+| easy | 65,536 | 29 | 1,900,544 | oracle run blocked before answer |
+| medium | 262,144 | 37 | 9,699,328 | not reached |
+| hard | 1,048,576 | 43 | 45,088,768 | candidate shipping preset |
+
+`escalate` multiplies the ambient width by four while keeping the 43-square
+answer fixed. It grows the haystack, not the certificate.
+
+## Local gate results
+
+| gate | result | measured evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 12/12 plants verified; 12/12 JSON round trips |
+| G2 | pass | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | tagged/fenced prose and raw JSON round-trip; garbage rejected |
+| G4 | pass | 0/200,000; exact structure-aware probability `1/2^42 = 2.2737e-13` |
+| G5 | pass | one valid answer among `2^42`; baseline 45,088,768 visits / 2.316047 s |
+| G6 | pass locally | six attacks each 0/8; reference sweep 8/8 as expected |
+| G7 | pass | doubled width 2,097,152 built in 0.060235 s and verified |
+| G8 | pass | 80/80 invariance, 80/80 carried witnesses, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | pass | 818 chars, about 205 tokens, 86 integer atoms, 281 operations |
+| G9(b) | **unproved** | no oracle call completed because the key's total limit was exceeded |
+
+The six failing G6 attacks are north-first, east-first, an alternating ansatz,
+following the level center, choosing the widest local interval, and 256 uniform
+random restarts. The full level sweep is disclosed separately as Track B's
+successful reference algorithm.
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+The script-owned `llm_loop_transcript.jsonl` contains four error records. It is
+infrastructure evidence, not hardness evidence:
+
+| preset | model | seed | outcome |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| easy | Claude Sonnet 5 | 668658390 | HTTP 403 key total limit |
+| easy | Claude Sonnet 5 | 1451769011 | HTTP 403 key total limit |
+| easy | Grok 4.6 | 826732900 | HTTP 403 key total limit |
+| easy | Grok 4.6 | 1070285932 | HTTP 403 key total limit |
+
+| G9 arm | solved / completed attempts | conclusion |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0 / 0 | unavailable; all calls were API errors |
+| structural hint | 0 / 0 | not run until the bare ladder yields a shipping preset |
+| placebo hint | 0 / 0 | not run until the bare ladder yields a shipping preset |
+
+Consequently hinted-minus-placebo is undefined. No `g9_*_transcript.jsonl`
+files were fabricated. After the OpenRouter limit is restored, rerun the bare
+ladder, set `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY` to its held rung, rerun `selftest`, then run
+the two G9 arms in separate scratch directories as required.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_2408_09272 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, render, parse_answer, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=3, **DIFFICULTY["demo"])
+print(render(inst))
+candidate = parse_answer('<answer>[[-17,12],[-16,12],[-15,12],[-15,13],[-14,13]]</answer>')
+assert verify(inst, candidate) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+Once the missing oracle/G9 evidence has been completed, emit from the repository
+root with `scripts/emit.sh 2408.09272 20 hard`. Do **not** emit the current
+provisional result as a shipped artifact.
+
+## Caveats
+
+- The difficulty claim is no-tool compression, not computational hardness. A
+  program that uses the interval ranks solves the target quickly; the module
+  says so explicitly.
+- `P(guess)` is uniform over every in-region north/east path from the marked
+  root. It measures blind path guessing after enforcing shape, start, length,
+  and region membership. It does not model a solver that discovers the rank
+  invariant.
+- The hard instances use a succinct interval representation. Expanding every
+  lattice cell is precisely the disclosed mechanical baseline; applications
+  requiring explicit-cell inputs should not quote the same compression gap.
+- The adversary panel does not include SAT/ILP encodings, transfer matrices, or
+  learned pattern detectors. Those are tool-assisted and outside Track B's
+  no-tool setting, but they could provide additional diagnostics.
+- The marked root lies inside a broad plateau of decoy roots with the same path
+  statistics, so it is not a per-root positional or degree outlier. This was
+  checked by construction and by the reported local attacks, not by a general
+  indistinguishability theorem.
+- Most importantly, the oracle and G9 results are missing because of an account
+  limit. The local gates alone are insufficient to trust or ship the family.
