codex
Built a provisional native Track B generator based on the paper’s root-ordering Lemma 1. The [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2408.09272) cites [Sheffield’s linear-area reconstruction algorithm](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0107095), which is disclosed as the reference algorithm.

Files:

- [gen_2408_09272.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/gen_2408_09272.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- 12/12 planted witnesses verified.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability \(2^{-42}\).
- Six attacks: each 0/8.
- Reference algorithm: 45,088,768 cell visits, 2.316 seconds on the measured instance.
- Compact route: at most 281 operations.
- Answer: 818 characters, approximately 205 tokens, 86 integers.
- Canonicalization: 80/80 invariance and carried-witness checks.

The result is not marked shippable: every required oracle call returned HTTP 403, “Key limit exceeded (total limit).” Consequently STEP 4 and G9(b) remain unproved, `all_passed` is honestly `false`, and no G9 transcripts were fabricated. Restoring the OpenRouter allowance and rerunning the harness is required to finish.
