-are measured in selftest; none uses the rank invariant."""
+NOTES = """Definition 1 gives one square on each of L consecutive levels.
+Section 2, Equation (2) states sigma_l=sum_{j=l-L+1}^l tau_j and proves that
+tau_l is independent of the tiling.  We sample Q=sum tau_l*x^l first and build
+S=(1+x+...+x^(L-1))Q by endpoint events.  Section 1 rules out Track A: it
+cites Sheffield's linear-area algorithm for simply connected regions, while
+complexity for general ribbon regions is open.  Track B reports the dense O(D)
+Equation (2) recurrence.  Its compact alternative is
+(1-x)S=(1-x^L)Q.  Positive-boundary, run-start, largest-jump,
+endpoint-pairing and random-polynomial attacks are measured.  Each sampled
