 ## Caveats
 
-- The difficulty claim is no-tool compression, not computational hardness. A
-  program that uses the interval ranks solves the target quickly; the module
-  says so explicitly.
-- `P(guess)` is uniform over every in-region north/east path from the marked
-  root. It measures blind path guessing after enforcing shape, start, length,
-  and region membership. It does not model a solver that discovers the rank
-  invariant.
-- The hard instances use a succinct interval representation. Expanding every
-  lattice cell is precisely the disclosed mechanical baseline; applications
-  requiring explicit-cell inputs should not quote the same compression gap.
-- The adversary panel does not include SAT/ILP encodings, transfer matrices, or
-  learned pattern detectors. Those are tool-assisted and outside Track B's
-  no-tool setting, but they could provide additional diagnostics.
-- The marked root lies inside a broad plateau of decoy roots with the same path
-  statistics, so it is not a per-root positional or degree outlier. This was
-  checked by construction and by the reported local attacks, not by a general
-  indistinguishability theorem.
