Implemented and locally verified a Track B generator based on Definition 1 and Equation (2) of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.09272).

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/gen_2408_09272.py:1)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/README.md:1)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results: all G1–G9(c) gates pass, including 0/200,000 informed guesses, five attacks at 0/8, 21,196,647 mechanical operations versus 160 compact operations, and a 144-atom answer.

The result is not yet shippable: all three easy oracle attempts solved, two medium attempts failed, then OpenRouter exhausted its total key limit before the deciding attempt. Both G9 runs likewise contain only genuine HTTP 403 error records. No hardness verdict was fabricated.

After restoring quota, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.09272
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2408_09272.py
```

Then update the shipping rung from the resulting verdict and rerun the two G9 scratch arms.
